# mti-fleet-monitor — environment.
#
# QUOTING: Bun's dotenv treats an unquoted `#` as a comment, so single-quote any
# password carrying `#`, a space or a quote.

# ── Database — the pg-relay, keyless (same as anomaly-detect) ──────────────
# The Cloud SQL instance is private-IP only; the app reaches it through the
# pg-relay on Cloud Run with per-request tokens. None of these is a secret.
# Identity comes from Vercel OIDC (enable it on the project: Settings →
# Security → Secure Backend Access with OIDC Federation, issuer mode Team)
# exchanged at GCP Workload Identity Federation for this app's service account.
PG_RELAY_URL=https://pg-relay-4d43xabdiq-el.a.run.app
PGDATABASE=nyk_mti
GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER=822457690126
GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_POOL_ID=vercel
GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_POOL_PROVIDER_ID=vercel
# anomaly-detect's account for now — this Vercel project must be allowed to
# impersonate it in the WIF binding, or give this app its own account.
GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=vercel-anomaly-detect@lifeosai-481608.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Local runs have no Vercel OIDC token: scripts/local.ts (and LIVE_DB=1 tests)
# use PGHOST / PGPORT / PGUSER / PGPASSWORD / PGDATABASE through scripts/wsproxy.ts.

# Pin the business (living_office.domain.slug). Unset = every vessel entity.
# DOMAIN_SLUG=eums

# There is no sign-in. Whoever reaches the URL reads this business — put the
# app behind a host that decides who can reach it.

# ── Host ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT is supplied by the LifeOS host; unset on Vercel (harmless — see config.ts).
# FRAME_ANCESTORS=https://preview.example.com   extra origins allowed to frame this
